### Order parameters

To further characterize the magnetic SU(3)-broken phase, we define the uniform magnetization of the unit cell \(m=|\sum_{i\in\text{unit cell}}\vec{\lambda}_{i}|\), \(\lambda_{i}^{\alpha}\) being the 8 generators of SU(3) acting on the site \(i\), giving the fraction \(m/m_{0}\) of the magnetization \(m_{0}\) of the fully polarized ferromagnet. As shown in the middle panels of Figs. 4, 5 and 6 the SU(3)-broken phase can be determined more accurately from the onsets of finite values of \(m\) which reaches its maximal value \(m_{0}=2/\sqrt{3}\) in the fully polarized ferromagnet.

